Z||000000||CW85T-Type||03-24-2000||04:26 PM||||Hi!  Just wanted to say I am a new Fiero owner.  Tuesday night I picked up my car from it's original owner who garaged it since new and seems to have taken good care of it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>1985 Fiero 2m6 with 120,000 miles.<BR>V-6, WS6 package, 4 Spd, White, A/C, no PW, PDL or rear defroster. Paint is near perfect and so is the interior. The best part is I only paid $1300 for it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'm using it to replace my 86 CRX DX that I have.  The CRX was a car that you get fatigued when you drive it alot of miles.  So far this Fiero has been more comfortable, with more power and better handling than my CRX.<P>I'm sure I will have lots of questions in the future.<P>Chris Wilson||||reg||10
Z||000001||zebrex||03-24-2000||06:38 PM||||congrats on the purchase and welcome the the forum. Im kinda new here too but I think you will like it here. sounds like you got a good deal||||reg||14
Z||000002||TheFiero64||03-24-2000||07:00 PM||||Good deal. Welcome to the fiero community. I know you will enjoy it. I love going on long trips with mine. I get out after a long drive and feel fine. In most cars I ache all over after a long trip.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Have fun and enjoy||||reg||10
